@page "/Error"

@* Lab adaptation (Sprint 33.9, FE33-052): the BeeDay source cascades the real HttpContext and
   reads Activity.Current?.Id ?? HttpContext?.TraceIdentifier to show the real request's trace id.
   Both are dropped — [CascadingParameter] HttpContext isn't provided by anything in the Lab, and
   fabricating a lookalike would misrepresent a real per-request value. RequestId is instead a
   fixed, obviously-synthetic placeholder constant.

   @attribute [AllowAnonymous] is also dropped: the Lab has no authorization pipeline for this to
   opt out of (Program.cs has no AddAuthorization/UseAuthorization).

   The BeeDay source injects IStringLocalizer<SharedResources> for every string below — dropped for
   plain hardcoded English strings taken verbatim from SharedResources.en-US.resx at extraction
   time. *@

<PageTitle>Error</PageTitle>

<h1 class="text-danger">Error</h1>
<h2 class="text-danger">An error occurred while processing your request.</h2>

@if (ShowRequestId)
{
    <p>
        <strong>Request ID:</strong> <code>@RequestId</code>
    </p>
}

<h3>Development mode</h3>
<p>The Development environment displays more detailed information about the error.</p>
<p><strong>Do not enable the Development environment in deployed applications. It can expose sensitive exception information to users.</strong></p>
<p>For local debugging, set ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT to Development and restart the app.</p>

@code
{
    // Sprint 33.9 (FE33-052): fixed, obviously-synthetic placeholder — not derived from any real
    // request (no HttpContext/Activity is available or fabricated here).
    private const string RequestId = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000";
    private static bool ShowRequestId => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(RequestId);
}
